;; Two controls of a prefix that declares code deleted, on prefixes and units
;; made by hand. The first is of the test that the tool makes of a prefix
;; before it uses one (prefix_fault in ../../tools/flsemantics.ml): no source
;; and no text makes a unit that binds, or declares deleted, a code id of
;; another unit, so the tool given a file does not reach these refusals. The
;; second is of the steps of a run: a prefix of declarations alone is one step
;; more, and the run ends as it did unless it ended at the last step that the
;; tool allows. What ../../tools/prefix_fault_control.ml prints is compared
;; with control.expected.

(rule
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   control.output
   (run %{dep:../../tools/prefix_fault_control.exe}))))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff control.expected control.output)))
